WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.840
Nothing in your business happens without
you, and it's starting to wear you down,

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:07.580
You're on your phone at all hours
answering the same questions, making the

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:12.320
same decisions, putting out the same fires
long after everyone else has clocked off.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.800
And you tell yourself this
is just what it takes.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.080
Every founder goes through it, but
that's the story that keeps you stuck.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.980
This isn't what running a business looks
like, it's what a business looks like when

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.710
everything still runs through you.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:27.280
I'm Nuno, and I help founders bring
structure to the chaos so the business can

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:29.990
run without them holding
every piece of it together.

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:33.970
Picture this, your team makes the
day-to-day calls, without coming to you.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:38.600
The same problem gets solved the same way
every time, whether you're in the room or

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:43.120
not, and you finally get to step back from
the firefighting and think about where

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:44.530
this business is actually going.

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:47.440
Let me tell you where most of the
founders are when they come to me.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.360
You've got a strategy in your head, things
you want to build, where you want to be

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:56.040
in five years, but you never get to any
of it because every day gets swallowed by

00:00:56.040 --> 00:01:00.310
the day-to-day. Approvals, questions,
decisions your team should be making

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:03.470
without you. Then you get to the end
of the day and ask yourself what did I

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:07.200
actually move forward? And
the answer is almost nothing.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.480
You were busy every minute, but
you were reacting, not building.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:12.810
If that's you right now,
that is the hard truth.

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:16.960
You don't own a business, you own a
job, one that depends entirely on you.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:20.700
And the moment you try to grow it breaks
because you can't be in every room at

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:24.080
once. The solution? The Vessel
Operating System method.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.140
So how do we fix it? A
bit of background first.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:32.240
I spent six years as an officer in the
Portuguese Marines, then seven and a half

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:36.160
years at Amazon building operations
where things simply had to work.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:39.800
Out of all that, I built my own
method of getting business in order.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:43.280
I call it the Vessel Operating
System, and it has three parts.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:47.620
First, the Bridge. That's your strategy,
where the business really is and where you

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:52.240
actually want to take it. Before anything
else, we get clear on the destination.

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:56.120
Second, the Hull. That's
what keeps you afloat.

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:58.570
Your systems, your processes, your cash.

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:02.760
This is where we build the structure your
team can follow so decisions stop coming

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:06.240
back to you. Third, the Cargo Hold.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:08.310
That's what the business carries.

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:11.110
Your product and how
you take it to market.

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:15.860
I score every part of it, so we see where
the real gaps are, not where you think

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:21.120
they are. Because often what you believe
is the problem isn't the problem at all.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:25.700
Then we get to work in focused 90-day
plans: a handful of projects at a time,

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.120
all measured, so you can see it working.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.470
And I don't hand you a plan and walk away.

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:34.390
You and your team do the building,
and I'm with you every step because

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:37.550
implementation is the part
that actually changes things.

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:40.080
Let me show you what this
looks like in practice.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:43.990
With the production agency, we got the
whole team aligned on where the business

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:48.760
was going and made the organisation
leaner and more efficient along the way.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:53.060
With that same agency, we improved their
communication systems and cut the time the

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:55.520
founder spends making
decisions by around 20%.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:01.040
And with a clinical psychology practice,
we defined a new service and worked out

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:04.280
exactly who it was for
and how to reach them.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:06.800
Now picture where this gets you.

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:08.480
Not just in the business, but at home.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:12.240
The founders I work with tell me
that's where they notice it the most.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:15.280
They sleep better, they are off their
phones in the evening, they've got time

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:18.400
for their family again and for
the things they used to enjoy.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:21.270
Because there's no real
line between work and home.

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:25.560
If the business is a mess, you don't get
to walk through the door and switch it

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.540
off, fix one and fix the other.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:31.440
So if that's where you want to
get to, here's the first step.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.890
Hit the button below
and book a call with me.

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:38.580
It's 30 minutes. It's a real conversation
about where you are at and whether we are

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:42.410
the right fit for each other. You'll
get a straight answer either way.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:46.620
This is hands-on work, so I only take
on a small number of founders at a time.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.170
That's how the quality stays high.

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:52.390
So if you are ready to stop running a job
and start owning a business, book your

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:56.250
call below. Thanks for watching.

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:57.880
Speak soon.
